notes.body:
@pquantin I took a closer look at how the isakmp dissector handles error conditions and I agree that adding expert items makes more sense than simply adding error messages to tree items. However, I would prefer to do it in a separate MR and keep this MR simple, i.e., just fix this annoying bug (and another one I found, see other commit.)

The refactoring would be too big, because I also need to change the isakmp dissector in order to make both dissectors as consistent as possible: For example, it does not make sense to add both, an expert item and a (redundand) error message to the dissected item, so I want to remove the latter.

During my experiments I also found a bug in the isakmp error handling: I forced a failure of the block size check to see the expert items in action...

```
diff --git a/epan/dissectors/packet-isakmp.c b/epan/dissectors/packet-isakmp.c
index efbd891089..c6c72e4837 100644
--- a/epan/dissectors/packet-isakmp.c
+++ b/epan/dissectors/packet-isakmp.c
@@ -5947,7 +5947,7 @@ dissect_enc(tvbuff_t *tvb,
     /*
      * Confirm encrypted data length is multiple of block size.
      */
-    if (encr_data_len % key_info->encr_spec->block_len != 0) {
+    if (TRUE) {
       proto_item_append_text(encr_data_item, "[Invalid length, should be a multiple of block size (%u)]",
                              key_info->encr_spec->block_len);
       expert_add_info(pinfo, encr_data_item, &ei_isakmp_enc_data_length_mult_block_size);
```

...which triggered a dissector bug: While reassembling the first fragment of the IKE_AUTH message (frame 3), the dissector ignores the null return value of `dissect_enc()` (assigned to `isakmp_decrypted_fragment_tvb`) and passes it to `tvb_get_guint8()`, causing an assertion failure in `epan/tvbuff.c`:

https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/c1082bd99ee0cd997df440dc19569e0208f03af4/epan/dissectors/packet-isakmp.c#L4673-4685

